        ":question/id": "1da4f94b-c6e6-57bb-95c9-efc33159af10",
        ":question/problem": "Find ${f}^{\u2032}(x)$ when $f(x)={cos}^{6}\u2061(x).$",
        ":question/worked-solution": "First, we express\n\n$$\nf(x)=(\\operatorname{cos}\u2061x)^{6}.\n$$\n\nNow, we see that $f(x)$ can be expressed as the composite function\n\n$$\nf={u}^{6},\\,u=\\operatorname{cos}\u2061x.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}u}=6{u}^{5}\\,\\text{and}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=-\\operatorname{sin}\u2061x.\n$$\n\nWe now apply the chain rule, and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{\u2032}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}u}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x} \\\\  & =6{u}^{5}\\cdot (-\\operatorname{sin}\u2061x) \\\\  & =-6{u}^{5}\\operatorname{sin}\u2061x \\\\  & =-6(\\operatorname{cos}\u2061x)^{5}\\operatorname{sin}\u2061x \\\\  & =-6{cos}^{5}\u2061x\\operatorname{sin}\u2061x.\\end{aligned}\n$$"
      },
      "role": "independently authored inventory",
      "relationship_to_source_templates": "Same unit sine blank / unit cosine complete five-choice profile / negative scaled cosine blank backbone as MA templates; retained verbatim, excluded from original-source fidelity counts."
